# Build context for deploy/accounts/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context root's `.dockerignore`,
# which is what lets the account service have its own without touching the repository's.
#
# The context is the repository root because the account service lives in the `mesh/` Cargo workspace
# and needs the workspace manifest. Everything else in this monorepo — five vendored upstreams and
# an Expo app — is irrelevant to it and would otherwise make the context several gigabytes.

*
!mesh/Cargo.toml
!mesh/Cargo.lock
!mesh/crates/**
# The entrypoint, which is COPYed into the runtime stage. Without this line the `*` above excludes
# it and the build fails at the COPY -- the whole point of an ignore file that starts by excluding
# everything is that a new file is invisible until it is named here.
!deploy/accounts/entrypoint.sh

# ...but not the build output, which is the largest thing in the tree and is rebuilt anyway.
mesh/target/
**/target/

# Jellyswarrm is a separate workspace and is not a member of mesh/Cargo.toml, so nothing here
# needs it. (It is excluded by the `*` above; listed for the reader.)
mesh/jellyswarrm/
